Llmpalooza's build of the CUTLASS headers it uses (D-053, D-057): adds
llmp/CMakeLists.txt, which the source lock adds as the component's
project. It compiles nothing: it names the kept header trees as one
interface target, which llmpalooza's own sm_121a unit
(src/kernels/ggml/moe_cutlass.cu) includes.

diff --git a/llmp/CMakeLists.txt b/llmp/CMakeLists.txt
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5c1f2a8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/llmp/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 llmpalooza contributors
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
+
+# Llmpalooza's build of the CUTLASS subset it uses (D-053, D-057).
+# third_party/patches/cutlass/ adds this file to the pinned CUTLASS tree, and
+# the source lock adds this directory. It builds nothing and runs nothing:
+# CUTLASS's own CMake, tools, tests, examples and Python packages are not
+# kept.
+#
+#   llmp_cutlass_headers  include/cute and include/cutlass (header-only
+#                           templates) and the one utility header llmpalooza's
+#                           unit includes, tools/util/include/cutlass/util/
+#                           packed_stride.hpp.
+cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 4.4.3)
+project(llmp_cutlass LANGUAGES CXX)
+add_library(llmp_cutlass_headers INTERFACE)
+target_include_directories(llmp_cutlass_headers SYSTEM INTERFACE
+  "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/../include" "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/../tools/util/include")
